 I was pondering what exactly proscribes various races
from being certain roles. In particular, it seems to me that
a character of any race ought to get to be a priest, if that's
what they really want. As it is, you're restricted to humans
and elves. Seems that gnomes/dwarves and even orcs
ought to be able to share in the worship of a god, since they
all can pray, etc.
 So maybe it's balance considerations rather than logical
ones. Any thoughts?



